<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq-section" id="process-faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="faq-header r-left">
      <div class="tag">Common Questions</div>
      <h2>What people ask<br>before they start.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>How long does a typical commercial renovation take?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Depends on scope. A 2,000 sq ft office fit-out typically runs 4–6 weeks. Larger multi-trade projects can run 8–16 weeks. We give you a realistic timeline in writing before work starts — not a best-case scenario, an achievable one.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>What happens if you fall behind schedule?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>We do not wait for permission to recover. We add crew, extend hours, and resequence trades. You hear about the problem and the recovery plan at the same time — not the problem first and the plan three days later when you ask for it.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>Can we phase the work to stay operational?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Phased execution is something we plan for upfront, not adapt to mid-project. We have managed renovations in occupied offices, live retail environments, and operational medical facilities. The key is building the phase plan before demo begins, not after.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>How involved do we need to be during construction?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>As much or as little as you want. We handle all day-to-day trade management, scheduling, and site decisions within the approved scope. We need your input on change order approvals and finish selections — nothing else unless you want it. You should not need to babysit this project.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item r">
        <div class="faq-question">
          <h3>Do you pull permits?</h3>
          <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>We advise on permit requirements for every project and can manage the permit application process. Permit responsibility — who is the permit holder and who pays the fees — is defined clearly in the contract scope before we start. No ambiguity on this.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

